fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the two commits carrying the io error kind through StoreDir failures.

Verdict LAND on this tip, e57ff8d.

Two rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND on two items: a doc block
that had landed on the wrong method, and a new variant added to an
exhaustive public enum under a patch bump. Both fixed; the enum is
non_exhaustive and the changelog states the compile consequence.

The reviewer verified the cap-std claim from source, not observation.
Every escape refusal goes through one constructor in cap-primitives,
io::Error::new(PermissionDenied, ...) with no errno, on the Linux
openat2 path, the FreeBSD path and the manual resolver macOS uses.
Every other error the resolver synthesizes is built from a rustix
Errno and carries one. Only two other errno-less PermissionDenied
sites exist on unix, reopen and networking, and neither is reachable
from any operation StoreDir performs. The discriminator does not
misclassify on 4.0.2.

Fail-safe direction: if a future cap-std attached an errno to its
refusal, a refusal reads as a fault and the consumer errors loudly. A
fault cannot start reading as a refusal without an errno-less
PermissionDenied from a reachable path, and none exists.

Mutations, each killed by a named test: rebuild the source from the
kind alone, losing the errno, killed at the mode-000 assertion of
a_refusal_and_a_permissions_failure_carry_different_kinds; drop the
kind half of refused_by_confinement, killed by the same test's
errno-less-Other assertion, added fail-first this round; a probe
matching every variant without a wildcard, does not compile.

Kind round-trip is preserved by construction on macOS and Linux:
from_raw_os_error and the original decode share one function.

198 tests with --all-features, clippy clean, fmt clean.

Follow-ups, neither blocking: io_error rebuilds an error every call
site already owns and could pass through; the permissions test is
root-hostile and leaks its fixture on failure.
